learnings:
  - 'The builder''s final report TRUNCATED at ~92k tokens (the known large-edit failure mode) — verifying state directly (build + file-existence + wiring greps + live endpoint smoke + portal validate) recovered full confidence without the report. This is the reusable mitigation: never depend on a big builder''s self-report; check the artifacts.'
  - 'A transient inbox=0 appeared once during verification right after a build, then never reproduced across 3 clean queries — almost certainly hitting the server in the window where a prior test''s serve process was still releasing. The lesson: when a flaky result can''t reproduce AND the unit test covers the logic, trust the test + repeated clean runs over the one-off.'
  - 'Agent-effect highlights match by SYMBOL not taskId, so the Tasks cards had to register by derived symbols (tags + blurb-parsed #symbols) to be drivable by an agent — the same seam lore/graph use. The live-agent ''theater'' only works because cards expose their symbols to the shared agentStore.'
